/* Roboto Regular + Bold, subsetted to Western European Latin
   (covers all accented characters used in Italian city/place
   names — Ò, À, È, Ù, Ì, etc. — plus the euro sign), loaded
   into jsPDF to replace the standard 'helvetica' font, whose
   built-in encoding is limited to ASCII/WinAnsi and corrupts
   any of these characters. Subsetted (fonttools) from the full
   Roboto font down to just the glyphs actually needed, keeping
   this file small despite embedding real font data. */
var PDF_FONT_ROBOTO_REGULAR_B64 = "";
var PDF_FONT_ROBOTO_BOLD_B64 = "";
